      "first": "Ainsi la connaissance des morphismes de normalisation \\inserted{généraux} est réduit à celle des morphismes\n\\diagram{\\begin{tikzcd}[\nampersand replacement=\\&, column sep=2.2em,\nexecute at end picture={\n  \\node[left=2.2em] at (\\tikzcdmatrixname-1-1.west) {$(148)$};\n  \\path (\\tikzcdmatrixname-1-1.east) ++(.12,0) coordinate (tail148);\n  \\path (\\tikzcdmatrixname-1-2.west) ++(.31,0) coordinate (overlap148);\n  \\path (overlap148 |- tail148) coordinate (end148);\n  \\path (tail148) -- (end148) coordinate[pos=.46] (head148);\n  % One continuous shaft bears two right heads; its second head crosses the target Pi.\n  \\draw (tail148) -- (end148);\n  \\draw (head148) ++(-.10,.05) -- (head148) -- ++(-.10,-.05);\n  \\draw (end148) ++(-.10,.05) -- (end148) -- ++(-.10,-.05);\n}]\n\\Pi_1M_{g,I} \\& \\Pi_1M_{g,I'} \\& \\text{pour }I'\\subset I,\n\\end{tikzcd}}",
